cation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Department of Endodontics is searching for a part time faculty at the Clinical Assistant Professor, Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Professor level. The position would involve clinical teaching of DMD candidates as well as participation in the DMD and Post-doctoral didactic curricula offered by the department. Faculty who have achieved ABE Diplomate status are also eligible to be a clinical attending in the post-graduate clinic. Eligible candidates must have a certificate of completion from a CODA accredited Advanced Education Program in Endodontic. Faculty will be expected to participate in scholarly activities and will have the opportunity to participate in the intramural faculty practice. The position will remain open until filled. Salary and rank will be commensurate with experience and training. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 24FA0045 Posting Open Date 01/17/2024 Posting Close Date 01/17/2029 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Requirements for this position include: A DDS / DMD degree from a CODA accredited school; certificate of completion from an advanced education program in Endodontics and an active New Jersey dental license.  Position will remain open until filled. Salary and rank will be commensurate with experience. Certifications/Licenses Must hold an active New Jersey dental license. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/219478 Campus Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) Home Location Campus Newark (RBHS) City Newark S