      "title": "Lecturer Fall 2025 (Recitations for CS110-CS170)",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Lecturer Fall 2025 (Recitations for CS110-CS170) Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Lecturer Fall 2025 (Recitations for CS110-CS170) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Starting: August 27, 2025 (must be available from 8/27/2025 to 12/23/2025 Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Lecturer Fall 2025 (Recitations for CS110-CS170) Department Computer Science Salary Details 2,777 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary Seeking motivated individual wishing to work part-time teaching Introductory Computer Science course recitations. The usual course load is two recitations per term. The duties are those involved in counseling students in the practical hands-on computer sessions and will include teaching remotely and/or teaching face-to-face, correcting assignments, consulting on programming problems, and grading examination papers. In addition to these teaching responsibilities, the position requires the scheduling of two lab support hours per week and one office hour per week during the term. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 25FA0436 Posting Open Date Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience A Bachelors Degree in Computer Science or in a related field is preferred although candidates with strong computer science background and teaching experience will be considered. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Although guided instruction will be given throughout the term, required skills include: • Familiarity with Windows / MAC OS X operating systems • Basic computer knowledge • Basic knowledge of programming in some language • Basic MS Excel knowledge • Good people skills • Proficiency with presentation software Teaching or tutoring experience is preferred. Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Starting: August 27, 2025 (must be available from 8/27/2025 to 12/23/2025 Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/249166 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Cam