    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273848": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Department of Medicine: Hepatologist (GI) Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Department of Medicine: Hepatologist (GI) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Department of Medicine: Hepatologist (GI) Department RWJ - Medicine Gastroenterolog Salary Details Minimum of $416,958 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary Clinical Care Responsibilities: Clinical practice with 90% effort focused on direct patient care in the practice of hepatology and gastroenterology. Clinical practice will be concentrated on diagnosis, monitoring, management and endoscopic procedures on patients with or being evaluated for clinical problems related to the liver. It will consist of 7 half-day sessions per week (5 half-days of outpatient clinic per week, one of which may be fellow’s clinic or gastroenterology focused clinic) and 2 half days of endoscopy per week (particularly patients needing screening for or management of esophageal varices but also general gastrointestinal upper and lower endoscopy including screening colonoscopies). 10 to 12 weeks of inpatient hepatology service at Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital, New Brunswick per year (20% effort). During the RWJUH inpatient service, 2 half-days of endoscopy or outpatient clinics will be performed in the AM). Note that for candidates who are trained in liver transplantation, there will be an option of 20% effort at University Hospital, Newark on the liver transplant services. This will consist of 5 full weeks of inpatient care (i.e. including weekend duties) (10% effort), one half-day of clinic per month and weekly attendance (by Zoom or in person) on the weekly afternoon liver transplantation conference (10% effort). Establish and maintain physician office hours in order to be accessible to new consults and follow up patients, adjusting as needed at designated GI offices. Be accountable for overall care of patients who are consulted or admitted (inpatient and same day procedure) under Physician’s name. Provide complete and timely consults as requested by other specialists. Provide clear instructions, explanations, and options available regarding diagnosis, treatment, medications, and follow-up to patients, family members, and other health care team members. Provide GI night and weekend on-call coverage during inpatient service (estimated at 2 nights per Monday – Thursday weekdays and 50% of weekends while on inpatient service and otherwise as is necessary to cover clinical needs. Attend monthly meetings with key personnel to review data, outcomes, protocols, policies, procedures, and staffing to continuously monitor and improve the care rendered. Attend departmental physician staff meetings, M&M Conference, liver masses/tumor board meetings, fellowship selection committee, and other departmental meetings deemed appropriate by the Division Chief or the Department of Medicine Chair Identify opportunities to participate in research trials and publications Safeguard patient confidentiality at all times. Limit work/patient related discussions to private areas. Complete required medical documentation included in patients charts in accordance with the Medical Staff Bylaws. Provide accurate and complete information required for billing Submit clinical charges and patient notes in timely manner. Effectively communicate with patients, family members, and other health care team members. Academic Responsibilities at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School Supervise and teach fellows, residents and housestaff, and medical students. Perform clinical or translational research or quality improvement and academic program building in areas of interest, preferably related to liver diseases. Pursue leadership activities in medical societies and associations, particularly in leading gastroenterology, endoscopy and internal medicine societies. Participate in or develop CME programs, especially as related to gastrointestinal and biliary malignancies, advanced endoscopy or other clinical areas of expertise. Participate in the academic activities of the Gastroenterology and Hepatology Division as well as the educational, patient care, research/quality improvement and other activities of the Department of Medicine. Attend Division and Department meetings including but not limited to faculty meetings, Grand Rounds and Fellow recruitment sessions. Participate in appropriate Department of Medicine and Medical School committees. Perform other duties as assigned by the Division Chief and/or Department Chair. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0154 Posting Open Date 02/19/2026 Posting Close Date 01/11/2027 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience MD/DO or equivalent. Certifications/Licenses Board eligible in Internal Medicine and/or Gastroenterology. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269548 Campus Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) Home Location Campus Downtown New Brunswick City New Brunswick State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption.  Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of Professional References (contact Info) Certifications/Licenses Personal Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: Non-Discrimination-Statement . In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination (NJLAD)