-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Institute for Quantitative Biomedicine ( IQB ) at Rutgers University is seeking highly motivated graduate students to participate in cutting-edge research over the summer. This is an excellent opportunity for students pursuing advanced degrees in biomedicine, bioinformatics, computational biology, or related fields to gain hands-on experience in a dynamic research environment. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 26FA0606 Posting Open Date 06/12/2026 Posting Close Date 01/07/2028 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Must be currently enrolled in a graduate program in biomedicine, bioinformatics, computational biology, or a related discipline. Strong interest in quantitative and/or qualitative approaches to research. Excellent communication skills and ability to work effectively in a collaborative research environment. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Commitment to ethical conduct of research Self-motivation and independence Good documentation habits Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277061 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus Busch (RU-New Brunswick) City Piscataway State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or