    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279802": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Industry Consultants Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Industry Consultants Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Industry Consultants Department Career Exploration & Success Salary Details 1,250 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees, based on position, which includes: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits Life insurance coverage Employee discounts programs For detailed information on benefits and eligibility, please visit: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/benefits/benefits-overview . Posting Summary The Industry Consultant Program engages working professionals with talent acquisition, recruiting, or related human resources expertise to provide individualized, employer-informed career guidance to Rutgers–New Brunswick undergraduate students. Industry Consultants supplement the University’s career-readiness education by helping students understand current recruiting practices, employer expectations, and strategies for obtaining internships and full-time employment. This is a focused, part-time co-adjutant appointment for professionals contributing specialized industry expertise during a defined academic semester. The assignment is limited to virtual student consultations, program training and check-ins, and occasional consultation with Career Success Strategists on current recruiting practices and employer expectations. Industry Consultants provide one-on-one virtual career consultations addressing: Resume development and review Interview preparation and strategies Internship and full-time job-search strategies Professional networking and LinkedIn Employer expectations and contemporary recruiting practices Salary and offer negotiation, when appropriate Each Industry Consultant will: Manage up to four 30-minute virtual student appointments per week, for a maximum of two advising hours weekly, Monday through Friday. Conduct appointments through the Rutgers Handshake virtual-meeting platform. Complete an initial virtual orientation and training session. Participate in one professional-development or program check-in per month. Serve as an industry-content resource to Career Success Strategists when consultation is needed regarding current recruiting practices or employer expectations. Maintain appropriate student confidentiality and comply with applicable program and university requirements. The appointment does not include a continuing student caseload, general departmental responsibilities, administrative coverage, or staff supervision. It concludes at the end of the designated academic semester. Reappointment for a subsequent semester is contingent upon program needs, satisfactory performance, available funding, and required university approvals. The stipend for this appointment is $1,250 per semester. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 26FA0725 Posting Open Date 08/21/2026 Posting Close Date 09/11/2026 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree. Currently working as a professional in a Talent Acquisition capacity (i.e. early talent acquisition, hiring, training, etc) within one of our 6 career interest communities. *Preference is given to higher appointment demand areas, including Engineering and Tech, Business & HR, Health & Life Sciences. Well-versed in resume development, interviewing strategies, and contemporary job/internship search techniques. Must be able to commit to 2 hours per week virtually. Exceptional oral and written communication skills. Strong customer service skills. Comfortable working in a virtual setting, interacting 1:1 with student clientele. Preferred Qualificiations 2 years of experience recruiting entry-level undergraduate talent for internship and/or full-time positions and/or 2 years of experience working with the undergraduate student population in an advising capacity. Familiarity with the Handshake Platform. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279793 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus College Ave (RU-New Brunswick) City New Brunswick State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption.  Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its