    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279969": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor of Surgery",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Research Assistant Professor of Surgery Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Research Assistant Professor of Surgery Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Research Assistant Professor of Surgery Department RWJ - Surgery Vascular Salary Details Minimum of $120,000 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School ( RWJMS ) in New Brunswick, NJ is seeking a full-time Research Assistant Professor of Surgery. The Research Assistant Professor will conduct research activities that support the strategic priorities of the Department of Surgery, contribute to the growth of departmental research programs, collaborate effectively within multidisciplinary teams, and maintain strong communication with faculty, staff, trainees, and administrative leadership. The successful candidate is expected to possess the expertise, technical skills, and scholarly experience necessary to make immediate contributions to their assigned research program with minimal additional training. Candidates should demonstrate a strong record of research productivity and a commitment to advancing the academic mission of the Department of Surgery through innovative and collaborative research. Appointment to the Research Track is contingent upon the availability of funding from grants, contracts, and other approved sources. Continued appointment is dependent upon sustained funding and satisfactory performance in research-related activities. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0687 Posting Open Date 07/23/2026 Posting Close Date 06/23/2027 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience The Successful candidate must have: Ph.D., M.D., M.D./Ph.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in a relevant scientific or clinical discipline. Demonstrated research experience and scholarly productivity, including peer-reviewed publications. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://j