    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267546": {
      "title": "Co Adj Non-Teaching",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Co Adj Non-Teaching Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Co Adj Non-Teaching Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Co Adj Non-Teaching Department Adult Autism Services Center Salary Details 23000-26000 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Rutgers Center for Adult Autism Services ( RCAAS ) Psychological Services Clinic ( PSC ) is seeking a part-time therapist to join our team. We are looking for a clinician who is passionate about working with neurodivergent adults, providing individual psychotherapy and potentially group therapy. The majority of individuals receiving services at the PSC have Autism, ADHD , and/or Learning Disorders (LD), with some also presenting with acquired neurological differences, such as a history of traumatic brain injury or stroke. The therapist in this role will have the opportunity to actively engage in PSC team activities, including: Didactic trainings led by clinical faculty Individual supervision with licensed psychologist Dr. Cohen Group supervision with Dr. Cohen, doctoral graduate students, and postdoctoral fellows Position Status Part Time Posting Number 26FA0044 Posting Open Date Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience A graduate degree in a field relevant to psychotherapy (e.g., LAC , LPC , LCSW , PsyD, or PhD) Licensure to practice psychotherapy in New Jersey, or eligibility and a clear path toward licensure. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications A graduate degree in a field relevant to psychotherapy (e.g., LAC , LPC , LCSW , PsyD, or PhD) Licensure to practice psychotherapy in New Jersey, or eligibility and a clear path toward licensure Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267535 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus Cook (RU-New Brunswick) City New Brunswick State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion