 Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Rutgers Business School is seeking individuals to assist with non-instructional assignments for its non-credit programs and centers. Successful candidates will provide assistance, guidance, research, and other duties as assigned (e.g., design, recruitment, curriculum development, course design, research, etc.) on a variety of topics, including, but not limited to: accounting, accounting information systems, financial accounting, government accounting, taxation, administrative studies, finance, economics, real estate, marketing, management, management science and information systems, operational management, strategic leadership, supply chain, and much more. Candidates may be responsible for, but not limited to, the following: Conducting research Preparing materials (e.g., presentations, proposals, documents, etc.) as assigned by the hiring manager Generate reports, summaries, and materials for distribution to internal and external entities Developing curriculum, course designs, and course material review Some positions may be grant funded. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 25FA1259 Posting Open Date 12/01/2025 Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Requires an advanced degree and at least one year of instructional/presentational experience, or a combination of education and experience. The degree requirement may be waived if a candidate is considered a subject matter expert in their field. A doctoral degree is preferred. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment May be required to travel between Rutgers-Newark and Rutgers-New 